\f2\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec3 1. Put the Sword Back into the Sheath\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 The investigation began with an image:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec3 Stop cutting everything apart.\strokec3 \uc0\u8232 \strokec3 Put the sword back into its sheath.\strokec3 \uc0\u8232 \strokec3 Plug it in \'97 and observe.\strokec3 \
The sword represents distinction.\
It separates:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 this from that;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 inside from outside;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 subject from object;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 true from false;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 positive from negative;\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 figure from ground.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec3 Distinction is necessary.\
But permanent cutting eventually destroys the field one is trying to observe.\
The alternative is not to abandon distinction.\
It is to suspend the next cut long enough to observe what the existing cuts\uc0\u8232 already reveal.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26 \cf0 \strokec3 \
CUT\
\uc0\u8595 \
PAUSE\
\uc0\u8595 \
OBSERVE\
\uc0\u8595 \
RELATE\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 The sheath therefore does not negate the sword.\
It changes its function.\
The blade becomes an axis.\
The cut becomes a seam.\
The point becomes a needle.\
