\f2\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec3 8. The Tree and the Two Crowns\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 A tree presents another dual architecture.\
Above ground:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26 \cf0 \strokec3 \
leaf crown\
\uc0\u8594  light\
\uc0\u8594  atmosphere\
\uc0\u8594  exchange\
\uc0\u8594  expansion\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 Below ground:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26 \cf0 \strokec3 \
root crown\
\uc0\u8594  water\
\uc0\u8594  minerals\
\uc0\u8594  soil\
\uc0\u8594  fungi\
\uc0\u8594  anchoring\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 The trunk connects two branching fields.\
One crown expands into light and air.\
The other expands into soil and material density.\
They are not identical geometries.\
They are coupled orientation systems.\
The tree also stores time materially.\
Its growth rings record changing conditions through accumulated structure.\
Time becomes trace.\
The visible body of the tree is therefore not only current life.\
It is also stored passage.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

\f2\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec3 9. The Seed and the Crack\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 Before the visible rupture, the seed already contains organized potential.\
The crack does not create the entire interior organization.\
It exposes a transition that was developing before it became visible.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b \cf0 \strokec3 The room existed before the crack.
\f1\b0 \strokec3 \
This sentence is retained as a reflection, not as a universal mechanical law.\
A crack may:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec3 expose;\
