\f2\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec3 11. What Is Not Seen When Looking\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 Every focus creates an exclusion.\
When focusing on the tree, the forest recedes.\
When focusing on the forest, the insect disappears.\
When focusing on the insect, the ecosystem becomes background.\
When focusing on the cell, the organism becomes an abstraction.\
This gives rise to a central NEXAH question:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec3 How can a description preserve awareness of what it excludes?\strokec3 \
Orientation does not require seeing everything.\
It requires knowing the boundary of the current view.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26 \cf0 \strokec3 \
VISIBLE RECORD\
+\
DECLARED BLIND REGION\
=\
ORIENTED DESCRIPTION\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

