\f2\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec3 16. Numbers as Traces\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 The earlier Numbermagic phase often treated numbers as if they were active,\uc0\u8232 resonant bodies.\
Series I and Series II did not support that as new mathematics or physical\uc0\u8232 theory.\
A more careful reading is now possible:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec3 Numbers are traces left by declared operations, measurements, groupings and\strokec3 \uc0\u8232 \strokec3 projections.\strokec3 \
Numbers do not need to be alive in a biological or physical sense.\
They can appear dynamic because the process producing them is dynamic.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\fs26 \cf0 \strokec3 \
process\
\uc0\u8595 \
measurement\
\uc0\u8595 \
record\
\uc0\u8595 \
number\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 \strokec3 The number is stable enough to travel between descriptions.\
It is therefore a powerful carrier of trace.\
But the trace is not the whole process.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf0 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa321\partightenfactor0

